# Declare the line-ending convention, because its ABSENCE is the bug.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set in this repo but nothing said what the repository
# stores, so committed blobs ended up with CRLF while tooling writes LF. Git then
# warned on every commit ("LF will be replaced by CRLF"), `git status` showed
# phantom modifications for byte-identical files, and — the part that stopped
# being cosmetic — a fresh `git worktree` checkout produced shebang scripts with
# CRLF, and Node's parser hit `#!/usr/bin/env node\r` and threw
# `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`.
#
# The one-time `git add --renormalize .` that accompanies this file is recorded
# in .git-blame-ignore-revs, so `git blame` and GitHub's blame view skip it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touched by the text filters.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.vsix binary
